backend/.installed
# Re-included script homes (see the `scripts` override below) previously inherited
# blanket coverage from that bare rule. Nothing sensitive is tracked there today,
# but keep local operator config and key material ignored explicitly rather than as
# a side effect of a rule whose real job was hiding the directory.
scripts/config.*
scripts/**/config.local.*
scripts/**/*secret*
scripts/**/*credential*
scripts/**/*.pem
scripts/**/*.key
scripts/**/id_rsa*

# ===================
# 其他
# ===================
tests
!deploy/tests/
!deploy/tests/**
CLAUDE.md
.claude
# TK override: this repo's own agent contract is tracked, so the upstream rules that
# hide it must be narrowed to the root path. Both `CLAUDE.md` and `.claude` are
# pattern-less and therefore match at ANY depth; keep that reach for nested/local
# copies (e.g. an agent scratch `CLAUDE.md` in a subdirectory) and re-include only
# the repo-root entries that are already committed. Inside `.claude/` the tracked
# surface is exactly the session hook, settings and the `skills -> ../.cursor/skills`
# symlink required by the constitution; `/.claude/*` re-establishes the wall so agent
# state (`worktrees/`, `mcp.local.json`, `history.jsonl`, `todos/`) stays ignored — it
# is the only coverage for those, unlike `tmp/` which line 90 already handles.
!/CLAUDE.md
!/.claude/
/.claude/*
!/.claude/hooks/
!/.claude/settings.json
!/.claude/skills
# TK override: upstream ignores a bare `scripts`, which (being pattern-less) matches
# a directory named `scripts` at ANY depth. TokenKey keeps load-bearing tooling in
# `scripts/` (preflight gates, sentinels, ops) and in per-skill `scripts/` dirs, all
# of which are force-added today — so a NEW checker or skill script is silently
# dropped from commits until someone notices. Keep the upstream line for parity and
# re-include TokenKey's real script homes. `.pyc`/`__pycache__` stay ignored by the
# dedicated Python rules below, so nothing build-generated becomes visible.
scripts
!/scripts/
!/skills/*/scripts/
!/.cursor/skills/*/scripts/
!backend/scripts/
!backend/scripts/resolve-version.sh
.code-review-state
#openspec/
code-reviews/
AGENTS.md
# TK override: same reasoning as the `CLAUDE.md` re-include above — this repo's root
# `AGENTS.md` carries the sync.sh-managed Codex/Antigravity block and is tracked,
# while the pattern-less rule keeps hiding nested/generated copies at any depth.
!/AGENTS.md
backend/cmd/server/server
deploy/docker-compose.override.yml
.gocache/
vite.config.js
docs/*
!docs/PAYMENT.md
!docs/PAYMENT_CN.md
!docs/ADMIN_PAYMENT_INTEGRATION_API.md
!docs/ASYNC_IMAGE_TASKS.md
!docs/BATCH_IMAGE_MVP.md
!docs/COMPOSITE_GROUPS.md
!docs/PLUGIN_DEVELOPMENT.md
!docs/channel-monitor-v2-safe-defaults.md
!docs/legal/
!docs/legal/*.md
!docs/screenshots/
# TK override: upstream treats `docs/` as an ignore-by-default area with a per-file
# allowlist, because upstream keeps almost no docs in git. TokenKey does the opposite —
# 98 tracked docs (every `docs/approved/*` contract, `docs/global/*`, `docs/ops/*`, the
# operator runbooks) are load-bearing and referenced by preflight gates such as
# `scripts/checks/approved-docs-index.py`, yet all of them were force-added past this
# rule. That makes a NEW approved design doc silently uncommittable, which is the same
# trap the `scripts` override above fixes. Re-include doc SUBDIRECTORIES (that is where
# TK organizes docs, and a brand-new home works without editing this file); loose files
# straight at `docs/` root stay allowlisted so local scratch notes are still ignored.
!docs/*/
!docs/DEPRECATIONS.md
!docs/README.md
!docs/agent_integration.md
!docs/spec-delta-*.md
docs/screenshots/*
!docs/screenshots/mobile-account-actions-menu.png
.serena/
.codex/
frontend/coverage/
aicodex
output/
.codegraph/

